          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A saline drip in hospitals is usually 0.9 % m/v"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.066,
            0.162,
            0.172,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "sodium chloride (common salt) in water. That means 0.9 g of salt in 100 mL of solution (Fig. 5.5). 0.9% saline solution is safe for blood and replaces lost fluids in the body."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
